# Edition 08: executable bounded entity relocation slice, separate from the v3 graph.
migration_lab='https://sovereign-data-monitor.paulcull.chatgpt.site/migration.html'
migration_guide='https://sovereign-data-monitor.paulcull.chatgpt.site/migration/migration-guide.md'
migration_prompt='''Entity relocation decision: keep legal entity identity stable while changing physical home. Use a lawful transition policy, snapshot plus continuous change capture, versioned tombstones, target-applied checkpoints, graph closure and an entity-specific source writer fence. Persist source fencing before activating the target; never flip routing back after target writes. Separate placement version, writer epoch, policy revision and resource data version. Migration consumes the capped bulk lane; guard and operational capacity remain reserved. The executable edition-08 slice uses isolated mig_* row envelopes and one coordinator; it does not migrate the original normalized business.* fixture or prove distributed fencing. Read Entity relocation before implementation.\n\n'''
migration_diagram='''<div class="diagram-scroll"><svg viewBox="0 0 880 370" role="img" aria-label="Gateway uses placement directory to route to Singapore or India services. A bounded background controller copies and catches up from Singapore to India under OPA policy."><title>Stable entity, movable physical home</title><defs><marker id="migration-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="#547760"/></marker></defs><g stroke="#547760" fill="none" marker-end="url(#migration-arrow)"><path d="M250 60 H340"/><path d="M445 95 V145 H220 V190"/><path d="M445 145 H705 V190"/><path d="M335 225 H385"/><path d="M565 225 H605"/><path d="M475 325 V265"/></g>'''+''.join(svg_box(*b) for b in [(30,25,220,70,'Business API gateway','Entity + idempotency key'),(340,25,260,70,'Placement directory','Home / epoch / readiness'),(100,190,235,75,'Singapore services + store','Source writable until fence'),(385,190,180,75,'Migration controller','Copy / catch-up / verify'),(605,190,245,75,'Mumbai services + store','Staging → epoch 2 authority'),(375,300,200,60,'Regional OPA','Export + import admission')])+'''<text x="32" y="352" font-size="11" fill="#60755e">Deployment boundaries to build; the local slice uses one FastAPI coordinator and separate stores.</text></svg></div>'''
add('entity-migration','Bring the legal entity home.','Technical design / Entity relocation · edition 08','Add Mumbai as a fourth physical store, move the India entity while source operations continue, then change authority once and account for old copies.',
call('Executable relocation workspace','<a href="'+migration_lab+'">Open the animated migration monitor →</a>. Hosted mode is a browser simulation. The unified development lab requires four CockroachDB containers and regional OPA. Earlier SQLite results are historical adapter tests, not deployment evidence. The existing 30-entity catalog and normalized business examples remain separate.')+
section('A lawful transition, explicitly modeled','<p>This isolated LE-IN-01 fixture permits Singapore before simulated t=600 and requires India afterwards. The clock advances only through the deadline control. It is a hypothetical policy change, not a statement of Indian law. The original India-only catalog example continues to reject Singapore. Registration creates a staging destination; it does not grant permission to serve or export data.</p>'+table(['Identity / authority','Before migration','After activation'],[['Legal entity','LE-IN-01','LE-IN-01, unchanged'],['Physical home','SG / Singapore','IN / Mumbai'],['Writer authority','Epoch 1','Epoch 2; SG durably fenced'],['Placement directory','Version 1','Version 2, ACTIVE only after target enable'],['Business keys','P-001, R-001, H-001, GLOBAL-001','Same keys and owner; no geographic re-keying'],['US payload','Zero','Zero']]))+
section('How business services use the new store',migration_diagram+'<p>Provision the India cell with its local database, business services, OPA, gateway, message transport, keys, observability and backup policies. The business gateway resolves legal entity to home and placement epoch, then routes privately to the regional service. Services recheck authority in their local transactions; gateway caches cannot authorize a stale writer. Retry a stale route only with a refreshed directory and the original idempotency key.</p><p>The proof of concept represents these interfaces in one FastAPI process. It uses four independent CockroachDB single-node containers in the unified Compose deployment. All local geographies are logical labels. This is not local HA or physical residency evidence.</p>')+
section('The movement and authority sequence',flow([('Prepare','Register India; verify entity, country, table and key restrictions; retain capture history.'),('Copy + catch up','Capture snapshot and sequence; copy bounded batches while source writes append changes.'),('Validate','Reconcile contents, row versions, tombstones, applied sequence and graph closure.'),('Fence + activate','Durably stop the SG writer; final drain; persist IN route as ACTIVATING; enable epoch 2; mark ACTIVE.'),('Dispose','Bounded old live-row cleanup; separately account for history, backups and audit obligations.')])+table(['State / failure','Required outcome'],[['Source write after validation','Invalidate validation and return to catch-up.'],['Destination paused during copy','No transfer; lawful source operations continue.'],['Crash after source fence','Detect durable fence on restart; remain unavailable until recovery.'],['Crash after IN route checkpoint','ACTIVATING blocks commands until target enable is safely resumed.'],['Old source route or transfer envelope','Reject stale authority/epoch, even after the gateway cache expires.'],['Deadline missed','Fail closed for affected SG reads/writes/export; show residual copies.'],['Attempted reverse routing after target writes','Reject. Recover forward or perform a new lawful reverse migration.']]))+
section('Transaction boundaries and operational priority',table(['Local transaction','Contents','Outside the transaction'],[['Source business command','Authority/epoch check + changed rows + versions + local journal + request receipt','Copy, cross-region policy decisions and remote acknowledgements'],['Snapshot','Consistent entity rows and source sequence','Bounded destination apply and cursor advancement'],['Target batch','Staging authority check + versioned row/tombstone apply','Checkpoint update; retry may repeat the batch'],['Source fence','Writable=false + final source sequence','Destination verification and route activation'],['Activation saga','Persist ACTIVATING route, then target writable epoch, then ACTIVE','No cross-store atomic transaction; crash can pause availability'],['Cleanup','Bounded source live deletes; final fixture journal/receipt/snapshot purge','WAL/MVCC/backups/archive disposal evidence']])+'<p>The PoC keeps its routing/job row in SG after business cutover, so SG remains a controller availability dependency; retiring that whole cell is not demonstrated. A pilot needs a resilient, appropriately located directory and regional authority state. One entity lock makes the small slice deterministic. An unrelated UK command uses a different lock and store; tests prove it can commit while the India lock is held. This does not prove distributed or performance isolation. The pilot must separate guard, operational and migration queues, relays, worker groups, connection budgets, retry paths and I/O admission. Migration takes capped bulk capacity and yields when measured foreground p99 or lock pressure breaches its budget.</p><p>The fixture scans at most 193 envelopes. At 100M relationships, replace snapshot materialization and final comparison with consistent range scans, per-shard capture/application checkpoints and partitioned manifests. Existing latency targets remain pilot hypotheses. Start with no more than 10% foreground p99 degradation against the same hardware and offered workload without migration; measure errors, tail latency and catch-up lag. Establish an explicit entity cutover-pause budget from measurements.</p>')+
section('Operational model adapter: what moves',table(['Business scope','Included in this slice','Pilot extension'],[['Party and ownership','Entity-private party plus global_party_id; relationship and party_relationship','Move private owner data; reauthorize minimal global identity separately'],['Product and servicing','Holding, contact, consent, preference, history','Maintain table/key/purpose constraints and aggregate visibility'],['Alternate identifiers','Party, relationship and holding IDs','Preserve owner-qualified keys and reference closure'],['Classification and sovereignty','Classification row plus parallel policy envelope','Versioned rule/fact/grant/placement metadata; deny precedence'],['Federation recipients','No recipient grants in the migration fixture','Handoff pending outbound intents and inbound projections without inventing entitlements']])+'<p>The executable adapter uses typed envelopes in mig_rows and validates parents before activation. It does not yet move the existing normalized business.* tables. Staging remains inaccessible to ordinary reads. A normalized adapter must load parents safely, enforce foreign keys, expose complete aggregates and preserve idempotency receipts. Moving one entity must not move another entity’s relationships or make all contact data global.</p>')+
section('OPA policy and API outline',code('''POST /v1/data/bank/migration/allow
{"input":{"operation":"transfer","country":"IN","elapsed":0,
  "deadline":600,"conflict":false,"home":"SG","target":"IN","phase":"COPYING"}}

GET  /api/migration
POST /api/migration/register | plan | start
POST /api/migration/copy | catchup       {"batch":8}
POST /api/migration/validate | fence | activate | cleanup
POST /api/migration/write               {"kind":"update","request_id":"unique","expected_epoch":1}
GET  /api/migration/read/IN
# Synthetic faults: pause, conflict, deadline, stale, rollback.
# Scoped reset: {"scenario":"synthetic-india"}. Conflicts return HTTP 409.
# API outlines above are implemented by the isolated local migration adapter.''','API / Rego input')+'<p>Inputs come from trusted coordinator facts. The module defaults deny for other geographies; an India exclusion blocks the transfer. Runtime route, epoch and staging checks complement OPA. Configure separate source and India OPA endpoints for export/import admission. An unavailable decision service fails closed. Signed bundles, authoritative fact freshness, optimistic control revisions, jurisdiction-aware administration and approval roles are pilot work.</p>')+
section('Change capture, telemetry and evidence','<p>The slice journals business changes in the same local SQL transaction. Extend this to an operational outbox plus region-local CockroachDB CDC and a durable message bus such as Kafka, with separate guard, operational and bulk lanes. Filter and authorize projections before any cross-border bus. CockroachDB CDC can duplicate messages and does not guarantee whole-transaction delivery order. Source resolved progress is distinct from target applied progress; preserve resource versions, tombstones, manifests and idempotency.</p><p>Migration spans carry bounded work.class values. Tests capture real OpenTelemetry spans in memory; optional OTLP/HTTP export and the existing Collector are wired but end-to-end export is unverified. Add per-shard lag, copied bytes, stale-write denials, cutover pause and cleanup-age metrics. Keep customer IDs out of metric labels and payloads out of global traces.</p><p>The monitor’s recent events are not immutable audit. Pilot audit uses regional transactional intents and an idempotent append-only relay recording authority changes, actor, policy versions, manifests and disposal evidence. COMPLETE means live fixture cleanup, not erasure from WAL/MVCC, backups, audit archives or caches. Retained surfaces and deadlines need their own evidence and exception workflow.</p>')+
section('Run and inspect the demonstration',code('''# Four CockroachDB stores, OPA, gateway and Collector:
./lab doctor
./lab up
# Open http://localhost:8080/migration.html
./lab smoke
./lab migrate --reset
# ./lab test executes the full CockroachDB acceptance gate.
# Hosted browser demonstrations do not run the container services.''','Run guide')+'<p>Start Auto-copy to validation and turn on the traffic generator, or manually add a party and relationship during copying. Inspect versions and journal lag. Fence SG, commit unrelated UK work, activate India, then update a holding. Try the old SG writer and stale transfer. Clean the source in bounded steps. Reset and try the deadline/exclusion faults.</p><div class="link-grid"><a href="'+migration_lab+'"><span>INTERACTIVE WORKSPACE</span><h3>Watch the relocation →</h3><p>Four stores, row versions, generator, gates and failure controls.</p></a><a href="'+migration_guide+'"><span>FULL ENGINEERING GUIDE</span><h3>Contracts, tests and extension points →</h3><p>Persistent runtime, Rego, transactions and pilot acceptance.</p></a></div>')+
section('Verified scope and pilot handoff','<p>Executed: browser state-machine assertions; actual SQLite persistence and restart; source-fence and activation crash-gap tests; HTTP read/write guards; real OPA integration; 24 Rego tests including 12 migration cases; OpenTelemetry span capture. CockroachDB execution, OTLP export, browser visual QA, WAN throughput, HA and production deletion remain unverified.</p>'+table(['Pilot work','Acceptance gate'],[['Regional deployment and database adapter','Run four-node integration; kill/restart DB, OPA and controller; handle serialization retries'],['Distributed authority','Competing controllers, stale service instances and partitions cannot enable two writers'],['Normalized graph and federation handoff','Full aggregates, pending outbox, receipts and authorized inbound/outbound projections survive cutover'],['Scale and workload isolation','50M-party / 100M-relationship workload with realistic skew and measured foreground tails'],['Disposal and operations','Live purge plus separately tracked backups/history; lawful exception and reverse-migration runbooks']]))+
section('Primary references',sources([('CockroachDB changefeed guarantees','https://docs.cockroachlabs.com/docs/stable/changefeed-messages'),('CockroachDB initial scan and cursor','https://docs.cockroachlabs.com/docs/stable/create-changefeed'),('OPA bundle distribution','https://www.openpolicyagent.org/docs/management-bundles')])),
migration_prompt+'''Implement StoreRegistry, PlacementDirectory, MigrationPlanner, SnapshotReader, ChangeCapture, TargetImporter, AuthorityFence, CutoverCoordinator and DisposalTracker interfaces behind regional Spring Boot APIs. Use an India transition fixture with four physical stores and stable owner/party/relationship/holding keys. Start from the supplied isolated adapter, then implement normalized-table adapters and outgoing/incoming federation handoff explicitly. Keep business transactions local and bounded. Persist per-shard cursors, retain capture history, compare current policy before export/import, apply versions/tombstones idempotently and verify complete graphs. Source fence must commit before target activation; transfer request receipts and preserve event IDs. Require conditional placement CAS and durable regional epoch enforcement; test two controllers and partial failures. Add OTel work-class spans and regional append-only audit intents. Include paused target, policy conflict, deadline, crash/restart, duplicate delivery, old writer, stale transfer, late source update, cleanup and reverse-migration tests. Do not claim single-node containers establish residency/HA or that SQL deletion erases backups. Keep measured, simulated and proposed behavior explicitly labelled.''')

for p in pages:
 if p['slug'] in ['index','placement','entity-model','architecture','gateways','transactions','service-transactions','work-isolation','engineering','pilot-plan','operational-model','observability','apis','project-context','platform','lifecycle']:
  p['body']=call('New · executable entity relocation','Add Mumbai and move a synthetic India entity through copy, catch-up, validation, authority cutover and cleanup. <a href="entity-migration.html">Read the migration design</a> · <a href="'+migration_lab+'">Open the monitor</a>. This isolated slice complements the original three-store examples; normalized-table migration is an extension point.')+p['body']
  p['prompt']=migration_prompt+p['prompt']
 if p['slug']=='index':p['kicker']='Operational federation / Design edition 08'
